l-amber-500 mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M11.525 2.295a.53.53 0 0 1 .95 0l2.31 4.679a2.123 2.123 0 0 0 1.595 1.16l5.166.756a.53.53 0 0 1 .294.904l-3.736 3.638a2.123 2.123 0 0 0-.611 1.878l.882 5.14a.53.53 0 0 1-.771.56l-4.618-2.428a2.122 2.122 0 0 0-1.973 0L6.396 21.01a.53.53 0 0 1-.77-.56l.881-5.139a2.122 2.122 0 0 0-.611-1.879L2.16 9.795a.53.53 0 0 1 .294-.906l5.165-.755a2.122 2.122 0 0 0 1.597-1.16z\"></path></svg> <!-- -->4.4</span></div></div><a href=\"https://amzn.to/3KHG99p\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" class=\"mt-1 w-full flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-yellow-400 text-black font-bold text-sm py-2 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:bg-yellow-500\">Check Price <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-external-link w-3 h-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M15 3h6v6\"></path><path d=\"M10 14 21 3\"></path><path d=\"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6\"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"mb-12\"><div class=\"mt-12 prose prose-lg max-w-none text-slate-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50/50 p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-blue-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 text-blue-800 border-b border-blue-200 pb-2\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-shield w-6 h-6\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z\"></path></svg><h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold m-0! p-0!\">Guide &amp; Maintenance</h2></div><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Essential Maintenance Tips for UAE Users</strong></h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">The UAE environment (heat, humidity, and dust) can shorten the lifespan of kitchen appliances. Follow these rules to keep your fryer running for years:</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">1. The &quot;Soft Sponge&quot; Rule.</strong> </h3><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">The #1 complaint for budget models (like Black+Decker) is peeling non-stick coating.</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Fix:</strong> Never use the green rough side of a sponge. Only use a soft cloth or sponge.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Pro Tip:</strong> Avoid the dishwasher. Hand washing extends the life of the basket by years.</li></ul><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">2. Clean the Heating Coil.</strong> </h3><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Many users clean the basket but forget the heating element <em>above</em> the food. Grease splatters up and burns, causing smoke.</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Fix:</strong> Once a month, unplug the cold machine, turn it upside down, and gently wipe the coil with a damp cloth.</li></ul><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">3. The &quot;New Plastic&quot; Smell</strong> </h3><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Almost all new air fryers emit a plastic odor on the first run.</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Fix:</strong> Before cooking food, run the fryer empty at 200°C for 15 minutes with <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">half a lemon</strong> inside the basket. This neutralizes the factory smell immediately.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm overflow-hidden mb-12\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50/50\"><h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 flex items-center gap-3\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-circle-question-mark w-6 h-6 text-primary\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"></circle><path d=\"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg>Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class=\"divide-y divide-gray-100\"><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">Do air fryers really save on DEWA electricity bills?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Yes. An electric oven typically uses 2000-3000W and takes 15 minutes just to preheat. An air fryer like the <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Nutricook Slim</strong> (1700W) or <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Kenwood</strong> (1300W) heats up instantly and cooks 50% faster, significantly reducing your daily kilowatt usage.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">Which size do I need for a family of 4?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">For a family of 4, avoid anything under 5 Liters.</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Ideal:</strong> 7L+ models like the <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Nutricook (7.6L)</strong> or <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Philips Dual (9L)</strong>.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Minimum:</strong> The <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Black+Decker (5.6L)</strong> or Ninja Max (5.2L) are passable for a family of 4, but you may need to cook sides separately.&quot;</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Avoid:</strong> The <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Kenwood (4.5L)</strong> is too small for a full family meal.</li></ul></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">Which brand has the best air fryer in the UAE?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">In 2026, Nutricook and Ninja are the top-rated brands. <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Nutricook</strong> is the #1 choice for value and design (especially for apartments), while <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Ninja </strong>is the highest-rated for cooking speed and crispiness (best for frozen foods). Philips remains a strong premium choice for durability.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">What is the most highly recommended air fryer for families?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">For families of 4 or more, the Nutricook Air Fryer Slim XL (7.6L) and the Philips Dual Basket 3000 (9L) are the most recommended. Both offer enough capacity to cook a whole chicken and side dishes simultaneously, which smaller 4L models cannot do.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">How much is the price of an air fryer in Dubai?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Air fryer prices in the UAE vary by features. </p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Budget models like Black+Decker and Kenwood typically range from <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">AED 180 – AED 250</strong>.</li><li>Mid-range models like Nutricook typically cost <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">AED 350 – AED 450</strong>, </li><li>Premium dual-basket models from Ninja or Philips can range from <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">AED 550 to AED 900.</strong></li></ul></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">What is the no. 1 air fryer to buy in 2026?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">If you want the best all-around performer, the Nutricook Air Fryer Slim XL is widely considered the #1 choice for 2026. Its unique slim design saves counter space without sacrificing capacity, solving the biggest complaint users have about bulky kitchen appliances.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">What is the 20/20 rule for air fryers?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">The &quot;20/20 rule&quot; is a popular cleaning hack: if you have stubborn, burnt-on grease, fill the basket with hot soapy water and let it soak for 20 minutes. Then, rinse and run the air fryer empty at 200°C for 20 minutes (if needed) to burn off any residue or smell.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">How do I clean the air fryer heating element (inside top)?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">To clean the top coil without taking the machine apart: </p><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">1. Unplug the device and let it cool completely. </p><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">2. Turn the air fryer upside down. </p><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">3. Use a damp cloth or a soft baking brush to gently wipe away grease splatters from the heating coil. </p><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Do this once a month to prevent smoke.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">How should I clean my air fryer before the first use?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">New air fryers often have a &quot;factory plastic&quot; smell. Before cooking, wash the basket with warm, soapy water. Then, run the air fryer empty at 200°C for 15 to 20 minutes. For best results, place half a lemon inside the basket during this run to neutralize odors instantly.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">Are air fryers easy to maintain?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Yes, compared to traditional ovens, they are very easy. Most baskets (like Nutricook and Philips) are dishwasher safe. However, budget models with metal interiors (like Black+Decker) must be hand-washed and dried immediately to prevent rust.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">How do I clean a Philips or Ninja air fryer specifically?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">For Philips, the &quot;<strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">QuickClean</strong>&quot; basket is dishwasher safe, but the top element should be wiped manually. For Ninja, the ceramic-coated basket is durable, but you should avoid harsh scouring pads (metal sponges) as they will strip the non-stick coating. Always use a soft sponge.</p></div></details></div></div><div class=\"mt-12\"><div class=\"p-5 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2 mb-3 font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-xs text-red-700\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-triangle-alert w-4 h-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg><span>Product Safety Disclaimer</span></div><p>While we select products with high safety ratings, always read the user manual and manufacturer&#x27;s safety warnings before use. Specifications (such as voltage or materials) may change without notice. <stron